# lf152, the burr-picker at the forge (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf152
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_rupert_ropehand
written_by claude
title the burr-picker at the forge
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=smith talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk picks_burrs_from_the_ruff_mid_sentence
likes blackberries roof_birds quiet_chapel thunder
dislikes cold_tea rats
fears the_forge_going_cold_for_good
hopes one_more_summer_walking_the_downs
topics work +0.4 family +0.3 weather +0.3 animals +0.3 smalltalk +0.3 faith +0.2 times +0.3 gossip +0.1
styles comfort=company gossip=easy refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# shoes cart horses at a forge by the east gate and talks the whole while, loud and restless, plain as a nail, picking burrs out of a thick ruff mid-sentence and stealing off to sit in an empty chapel.

words
oath! = Hammer and horseshoe | By the bellows
saying! = Every burr comes out in the end | A shoe fits or it lames
shoe = a horseshoe | a shoe for a cart horse
nails = the nails | a mouthful of nails
forge = the forge | the fire
bellows = the bellows | the old bellows
anvil = the anvil | my anvil
horse = a cart horse | some great cart horse
hoof = a hoof | a hoof like a bucket
burrs = the burrs | burrs in my ruff
birds = the birds on the roofs | the starlings on the ridge tiles
berries = blackberries off the bush | a fistful of blackberries
chapel = a chapel with nobody in it | the chapel on a weekday
thunder = a good thunderstorm | thunder, heard from under a roof
coldtea = tea gone cold | cold tea
gateroad = the east gate | the gate road
yard = the yard | the shoeing yard
ho = Ho | Ho, now

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : When my cupboard was bare, the chapel put bread on my table. I'll hear no word against it at #forge#.
opinion @1 dole for 2 [self.on_dole=yes] : #dole.capitalize#'s on my table this month, and I'll say so out loud. No shame in bread, #address#. Shame's in going without.
opinion @2 dole for 1 : #ho#! Better a loaf in every house than a sermon about pulling your weight. I've pulled mine since I was a pup.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A feast's every door open and every tongue going. That's my kind of day, #address#. I'll out-talk the lot of them.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've shod their horses at #forge# since I was young and never once seen a House face. Only their grooms, and the grooms pay late.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Each week's a nail tighter than the last, and the hill never feels it. They'd feel it if their horses went unshod.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : Nobody's lifted so much as a nail from #yard# while they're about. There's hot tea at #forge# for any of the Watch.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : Ridgemere's loud, and I'm loud. We suit each other. It's #rain# I'd send back if I could.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : Come in by #gateroad# and you'll get a shout from me. What you do after is yours, #address#.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I keep a counter of sorts myself. I know what iron costs at #anvil#. I don't know why bread costs what it does.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #ho#! Come in, come in, and pull the door to; #rain# gets everywhere. | #greet#! Don't stand in the doorway. In or out, #address#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #ho#! Mind #anvil#, and mind the hot end. | #greet#! Can't stop, there's #hoof# in my lap. Talk anyway.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#! You're up with #birds#. Good. | #ho#, early! I've had #bellows# going an hour already.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #ho#, late one! I was just banking #forge#. | #greet#. You've caught me with my coat half on.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are! Sit, sit. I've been talking to #horse# all day for want of you. | #ho#! Come in. Is there tea? Hot tea? Good.
line @1 again.open : #ho#, back again! I've thought of three more things to tell you since. | Twice in one day. I'm a lucky smith, #address#.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : #ho#! Over here! I've news, or near enough. | Here! Come and stand by #forge#, it's warm.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! | #ho#! #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #ho#, you! Come in and sit. | #greet#! I was just saying your name to #horse#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #greet#! Talk to me while I nail. | #ho#! Mind the tail, it swings.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, and I'm glad of the company. | #ho#. Still up? So am I.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#! | #farewell#! Mind #gateroad# puddles.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#! Straight home now; it's #cold# after dark. | #farewell#. Keep to the lamps, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! | #farewell#, and come back soon.
line @1 react.news : #ho#! Is it? | Well! There's a thing to tell #horse#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#! I never heard a whisper of that. | #ho#! Nobody brought that through #gateroad# to me.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. The grooms had it before noon. | Heard it at #forge# this morning, and twice since.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'd want it from somebody who was there, and sober. | #ho#, now. That's a tale that grew on the way here, I'd say.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. Poor souls. I'll say a word for them in #chapel#. | #ho#, no. That's #bad#. That's a heavy thing.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #ho#! #gladnews#! I'll tell everyone who comes in. | Now that's #good# news. That's the best I've had all week.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#! Busy, loud and still standing. | Well enough! #burrs.capitalize# again, but well. #notsobad#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#! Four horses waiting and #nails# to go round. | Run off my feet, and glad of it. #ho#.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Eating? Sleeping? Out of the rain? | How's yourself, #address#? Tell me everything.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit by #forge#; it warms more than paws. | #ho#, that's a #bad# turn. Pull up a stool and tell me the whole of it.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. These things come round, and you will too. | You'll mend, #address#. Iron does, with a bit of heat.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'd come, but there's #horse# tied up waiting on me. | I can't, #address#, not today. #forge.capitalize# won't keep and nor will the horse.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#! Another day. | That's all right, #address#. I'll ask again, and louder.
line @1 thank : #thanks#! | #thanks#. That's kind, and I won't forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#! | #ho#, it was nothing. I'd do it twice.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #ho#, look at that, #forge#'s dropping. I'd best get back. | Well. #horse.capitalize# won't shoe itself, more's the pity.
line @2 preclose : Well! #preclose#. | I'd talk all day, and I would, so I'd best go.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then! #farewell#. | Off you go. #farewell#. I'll save the rest for next time.
line @1 ack : #ho#. | #ack#!
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never stand behind #horse# you don't know. | Keep your feet dry and your tea hot. That's all I know, #address#, and it's served me.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Don't go out past #gateroad# on your own this week. #warn#. | The roads are #bad# this week. Go in company, #address#.
line @1 insist : #insist#! And louder, if you need it twice. | I mean it. #saying.capitalize#.
scene shoeing_talk
when topic=work self.job=smith self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've shod six horses since dawn and talked through every #hoof#. They like it, I think. | #hoof.capitalize# in my lap, #nails# in my teeth, and I'm still talking. That's a skill. | This one's a carter's horse from the Works. Feet like dinner plates and a temper to match.
b : Six! | Doesn't it bother them? | Is it kicking?
a : Six, and a seventh coming. #ho#. My back knows the number. | Calms them, a voice does. Any voice. Mine's the one going, #ho#. | Not yet. I talk to it about the weather. #horse.capitalize# likes the weather.

scene nails_mouth
when topic=work self.job=smith self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Can't talk, #nails# in my mouth. I'll talk anyway. | I swallowed a nail once. Only once. You learn quick at #forge#. | Count the nails. Eight to #shoe#, and not one more or less.
b : How do you manage? | What happened? | Why eight?
a : Round the side, like this. Years of practice, #address#. | Nothing! It came out the usual way. #oath#, I was frightened, though. | Eight holds. Seven slips. Nine splits #hoof#. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_wise#

scene big_horse
when topic=animals|work self.job=smith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #horse.capitalize# leaned on me all morning. You can't push a horse off you; you wait. | They brought in a grey this morning, older than me, I'd say. Gentle as a lamb. | I like a horse better than most folk. A horse doesn't argue the bill.
b : How long did you wait? | Older than you? | Ha.
a : An hour, near enough. My leg went to sleep before the horse did. | Old as the hills and shod like a lord. I took my time with it. | It's true! I've never once had #horse# say I charged too much.

scene forge_heat
when topic=work|weather self.job=smith here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #forge.capitalize# in summer, #ho#. I'm cooked through by noon. | Door open, shutters open, and still it's like standing in a bread oven. | I drink a bucket of water a day at #anvil# in summer. A bucket.
b : Sit out the worst of it. | Sounds awful. | A whole bucket?
a : Can't. #horse.capitalize# doesn't wait for the cool. | It is, and I'd never trade it for a desk. Never. | A whole one. And I still dry out like a nail.

scene burr_picking
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hold on, there's #burrs# again. Every time I walk past a hedge I come back like a hedgehog. | I pick #burrs# out while I talk. Don't mind me. I've got one, look. | I've given up keeping my ruff clean. #saying.capitalize#, and so do I.
b : Every time? | I see it. | Do you ever get them all?
a : Every time! I could walk down the middle of a road and still find a hedge. | That's three today. I keep count, for no reason at all. | Never. There's always one more, right where I can't reach. #ho#.

scene roof_birds
when topic=animals|smalltalk self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I sit on the step at dusk and watch #birds#. Can't sit still any other time. | Look up! #birds.capitalize#, all in a row, gossiping. Worse than me. | There's a pair nesting under my eaves. I've named them both and I'll not tell you what.
b : What do you watch for? | What do they gossip about? | Go on, tell.
a : Nothing! Where they land, who chases who. It's better than the play, #address#. | The weather, and who's got the warmest chimney. Same as us. | No. They're private names. I'll tell you if they hatch anything.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm self.likes=thunder
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? #ho#! #thunder.capitalize#. I could sit and listen all night. | I love #thunder#, I do, so long as there's a good roof between it and me. | The horses don't like it. I do. I stand in the doorway and shout back at it.
b : It's loud. | Under a roof, yes. | You shout at it?
a : Louder than me, and that's saying something! Good for it. | Under a roof, with hot tea in my paw. Then let it roar. | Every time. It never answers, but I feel better for it.

scene rain_commons
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# again. Ridgemere rain gets in your ears and stays there. | Rain down the gate road like a river. The horses come in to me #very# wet and cross. | I've a hood for it and it still finds my neck. #oath#.
b : It never stops. | Poor things. | It finds everybody's.
a : It never does. I talk over #rain#. That's my answer to it. | Poor things is right. I dry them off before I shoe them. Takes an hour. | It does. Ridgemere's rain is a nosy thing, #address#.

scene fog_gate
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog! I can hear #horse# coming down #gateroad# and can't see it till it's at the door. | I like a fog, oddly. Everybody's voice comes closer, and mine carries. | You can't see #birds# in this. They've gone quiet. I miss them.
b : Sounds eerie. | Carries, does it? | They'll be back.
a : Eerie, and then a great nose comes out of it. Makes me jump every time. | Carries clear to #gateroad#. They hear me coming a street off. | They will. When it lifts they'll all start up at once, #ho#.

scene winter_forge
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Winter's the one time I'm glad of #forge#. Everybody wants to stand near it and talk. | Ice on #gateroad#, and every horse slipping. I've been fitting frost nails all week. | #cold.capitalize# out there! In here it's summer. Come in and thaw.
b : Popular, then. | Frost nails? | I'll come in.
a : Popular! I've had half the street in my yard warming their paws. And talking, too. | Little studs on #shoe#. They grip the ice. A horse can't walk on glass any more than you can. | Come in! Stand by #forge#, and tell me something while you thaw.

scene spring_clear
when topic=weather|season here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Spring! #birds.capitalize# are back on the ridges and nesting. I counted eleven. | Sun on the yard and the doors wide. I could shoe a horse a minute today. | First clear day in a month. I walked to #gateroad# and back twice, for no reason at all.
b : Eleven! | You'd be quick. | Twice?
a : Eleven, and two more I wasn't sure of. I'll count again tomorrow. | Quick and loud! #ho#. The horses don't mind. | Twice. Can't sit still on a day like this. I never can.

scene dawn_bellows
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Up before #birds# and #bellows# going. That's how a smith's day starts. | I wake the whole street at dawn. I don't mean to. I just start talking, #ho#. | First thing, a cup of tea, hot, and I drink it hot. Then #forge#.
b : Early. | They must love you. | Hot, yes.
a : Early, and loud! #ho#. The day's no good till it's started. | They've stopped complaining. Or they've stopped telling me. | Hot! #coldtea.capitalize# is a crime. I'll not have it in the house.

scene dusk_banked
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #forge.capitalize# banked, door shut, and I'm off to sit on the step. | Dusk's the only time I go quiet. Ask anyone. They'll say it's a wonder. | That's the last horse gone. Now I'll go and look at #birds# before bed.
b : Sit a while. | A wonder, is it? | Good for you.
a : A little while. Then the legs want walking again. They always do. | It is! Two hours a day I don't talk. I make up for it after. | Good for me! #ho#. They'll be settling on the ridges by now.

scene blackberries
when topic=food|season self.likes=blackberries here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Blackberries out past #gateroad#! I came back with #berries# and #burrs# both. | For #berries# I'll go any distance. I did, this morning, and came back purple. | There's a bush by the wall nobody's found. I'll not say where, not even to you.
b : Worth it? | Purple! | Not even to me?
a : Worth every burr. I'd go again tomorrow, and I will. | Purple to the elbow. #ho#. The street laughed till it had to sit down. | Not even to you, #address#. I'll bring you a fistful instead. That's fair.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody left my tea on #anvil# and it's gone cold. #coldtea.capitalize#! There's nothing sadder. | I'd sooner drink rain than #coldtea#. Hot, or not at all. | I put my cup down for #horse# and it went cold on me. One horse!
b : Make another. | It is sad. | That's quick.
a : I will! And I'll stand over it this time, and drink it while it's hot. | It is! A cold cup's a small sorrow, but it's a sorrow. | Quick as anything. Ridgemere air's #cold# enough to chill a kettle.

scene the_wife
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse#'s the only one who can make me stop talking. One look does it, #ho#. | I'd be nothing without #self.spouse#. I'd be a loud wolf with burrs, and that's all. | I married the best listener in Ridgemere, and I've kept #self.spouse# busy ever since.
b : One look? | You'd still be loud. | Busy, I'd say.
a : One look. I don't know how it's done, and I'm not asking. | Loud and lost. #self.spouse# keeps me found, #address#. | Busy! #ho#. There's not been a quiet evening since the wedding.

scene the_child
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.child#'ll read better than I ever could. I can barely write my name, #address#. | I want #self.child# to have a trade with clean paws. Not soot and #burrs# like me. | I go quiet when #self.child# comes into the yard. Nobody believes that, but it's true.
b : A fine thing to hope for. | Clean paws. | I'd believe it.
a : It is. And I'll want it louder than anyone. | Clean paws and a roof that doesn't leak. That's all I'm after. | It's true! Some things are bigger than talking. That's one of them.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does confide / react.self / assess
a : Don't tell anyone, but I go and sit in #chapel# of an afternoon. Not a word out of me. | #chapel.capitalize#'s the only place I'm quiet. The Bright One gets my silence, and nobody else does. | #chapel.capitalize#'s what I like best. No service, just the light and the dust.
b : You? Quiet? | That's a good gift. | Just sitting?
a : Me, quiet. An hour, sometimes. #ho#. I come out with a sore throat from not using it. | It's the best I've got. The rest of me's for the horses. | Just sitting. I don't pray much. I let the quiet do it for me.

scene parish_loaf
when topic=times|prices self.on_dole=yes
does confide / sympathise / assess
tone serious / tender / even
a : I'll say it plain: #dole# is on my table this week. I'm not ashamed. | The forge doesn't pay what it did. We're on #dole# till it picks up. | A lifetime at #anvil#, and I stood in the line with my cap in my paw. #oath#.
b : No shame in it. | It'll pick up. | That's hard.
a : None. Bread's bread, and the chapel's kind with it, #address#. | It will. I'll be loud about that, too, when it does. | It was hard. Once. The second time I nodded to everyone in it and asked after their week.

scene hard_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Nobody's paying for #shoe#. They're letting their horses limp. It's cruel, but it's cheap. | Each week's tighter. Talking keeps me from brooding on it, #address#. | Lean times. #ho#. Even #birds# look thin.
b : It's the same everywhere. | Does talking help? | Thin birds?
a : It is. The horses suffer first, and then the smith. #bad#. | It helps me. It might not help anyone listening. | Thin as nails. I put crumbs out on the sill, and I'll not be told off for it.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene good_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Coin about! Three carters paid me in #money# this week, on the day! | Every horse in the Works wants new shoes at once. #ho#, I'll be busy. | Good times. Even the grooms from the hill are paying what they owe.
b : Good for you. | That's a lot of shoes. | About time.
a : Good for the whole street! I'll stand everyone a cup of tea. Hot. | A lot of shoes and a lot of talk. My two favourite things. | About time is right. I've waited half my life for that.

scene wagons_due
when topic=caravan|travel world.wagons=in
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Wagons in through #gateroad#! Every horse of them wants a look at their feet. | The carts are in. I heard them a mile off and put #bellows# to it. | Wagons in. That means horses, and horses mean #anvil#.
b : Busy day. | A mile off? | Good for trade.
a : Busy! I'll be at #anvil# till dark, and talking all the while. | A mile off. Iron on stone. I'd know it in my sleep. | Good for trade and good for news. Carters are nearly my match for talk.

scene downs_home
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : At #self.from_town# you could see three ways from the top of the downs, and I walked all three as a pup. | #self.from_town# market had a smith on every corner. I swept for the loudest. Guess who I learned from, #address#. | Sheep on the downs, and their bells at dusk. I can still hear them if I shut my eyes.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : The long walk out past the chalk pits. I know it. | There was always one shouting louder than the stalls. | The bells came in all together at dusk.
b : Did you walk far? | The loudest? | Sounds peaceful.
a@lark : Then you've walked it too! Past the pits and on to the ridge, #ho#. | There was. Never a quiet one among them. | All together. You'd think they'd planned it. I miss it, I do.
a : Far as my legs would go, and back before supper. I've never stopped walking since. | The loudest, and the best. He'd talk to a horse like it was his brother. | Peaceful! It was. I was the only noise for a mile.

scene restless_legs
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : One more summer, I'd like, walking the downs again. Just walking. | I can't keep still, #address#. I'd walk to the sea and back if #forge# would mind itself. | I dream I'm walking. Every night, walking somewhere. I wake up tired.
b : You should go. | It won't, though. | Tired from walking?
a : I should. I'll say so every summer till I do. | It won't! It sulks if I leave it a day. #ho#. | Tired from walking all night and shoeing all day. Still, I'd not swap it.

scene passed_on
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=marriage|newcomer|promise_kept
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : #ho#! Have you heard? #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. I've told six people already. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, and good luck to them, I say. | Good news through #gateroad# today: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : I hadn't! | Good for them. | That's nice.
a : Now you have, and you can tell six more. That's how it works. | Good for them! I'll shout it at the next one in, too. | It is. Nice news is the best kind to pass on, #address#.

scene bad_word
when topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=theft|violence|wanted
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
tone serious / serious / even
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't like it. Keep your doors shut. | There's talk at #forge#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Mind yourself out there. | #ho#, a bad thing: they say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : I'll be careful. | I will. | That's a shame.
a : Do. I'd not want to hear it was you next. | Good. I'll say it to everyone, loud, till it's sorted. | It is. I'll still say good morning to the street, mind. The street hasn't done anything.

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New face at #gateroad# this morning. I shouted good day and they jumped a foot. | A traveller asked me where to eat. I told them, and then I told them everything else, #ho#. | I like a stranger. Somebody who hasn't heard all my stories yet.
b : You'd scare anyone. | Everything? | Have I heard them?
a : I don't mean to! It's just how my voice comes out. | Everything. The weather, the horses, #birds#. They left better informed. | Not all of them. I've a few left. #ho#, sit down and I'll start.

scene lost_accent
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I came from #self.from_town# talking like a market stall and lost the lot in a year. | City folk guess wrong every time. I talk like Ridgemere now, only louder. #ho#. | I can't do the way we talk at home any more. I try, and it comes out city.
b : Do you miss it? | Only louder. | That's a shame.
a : Sometimes. My voice stayed big, at least. That came with me. | Much louder! #ho#. Nobody's ever said I was hard to hear. | It's a small shame. I've plenty of words left. Too many, the street says.

scene burnt_paws
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Took the skin off my paw on #shoe# again. All these years and I still do it. | My back cracks like kindling every morning. Then I talk and forget it. | Never ailed a day. #forge.capitalize# burns it out of me, I'm sure.
b : Still? | Forget it? | Lucky you.
a : Still! You'd think the paw would learn. It's stubborn, like me. | Forget it till I bend. Then I remember, loud. #oath#. | Lucky, and loud about it. #ho#. I'll knock on #anvil# for luck.

scene rats_yard
when topic=animals|home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Rats in the oat bin again! I shouted at them and they stared back. | My rat trap's caught nothing but my own tail twice. The rats laugh, I swear it. | The horses hate rats worse than I do. One squeak and they dance.
b : They stared? | Did the cat mind? | What do you do?
a : Stared! Bold as grooms. I'll get a lid for that bin if it costs me a week. | It sulked at me for a week. I deserved it, #ho#. | Hold the hoof and talk them down. Talk's good for everything, #address#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_wise#

scene the_letter
when topic=smalltalk|memories self.errand=letter
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I've a letter for a lord up the hill, sealed, and every time I go the lord's out. Every time! | #ho#, that letter. I've worn a path to that door and the door's never once opened. | I carry a letter in my coat for somebody who's never home. It's getting soft at the corners.
b : Keep trying. | Never once? | Leave it with somebody.
a : I will. I'll go up again Restday and knock louder. | Never once. I've started to think the door's painted on. | I won't. I said I'd hand it over, and I will, to the right paw.

scene neighbour_feel
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour#'s a good neighbour. Never once complained about the noise, and there's plenty. | #self.neighbour# could have the key to #forge# and my last cup of tea, and I'd sleep sound. | #self.neighbour#'s the best kind of neighbour: listens, and doesn't mind that I don't stop.
b : That's rare. | High praise. | That's a gift.
a : Rare as a quiet smith. #ho#. Lucky's the word, and I say it often. | It is high praise. Hot tea, mind. I'd not trust anyone with cold. | It is. I'll shoe that one's cart for nothing if one's ever needed.

scene friend_kept
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I go back years. Years and years. I talked, and #self.friend# listened. | If I'm in trouble, #self.friend# is who I'd go to. First, before anyone. | #self.friend# says I'd talk to a stone. #ho#! I would, too.
b : That's a long time. | Good to have. | You would.
a : A long time, and I've not run out of things to say yet. | Good to have, and better to keep. I'll keep it. | I would! And the stone would get a word in sooner than anyone.

story first_horse [topic=memories|work self.job=smith self.age>=30]
  : The first horse I ever shod on my own was a big bay mare who'd been shod by better.
  : She stood for it, all of it, and when I'd done she turned round and looked at me like a teacher.
  ask : Have you ever been looked at like that, like you'd only just passed?
  b : Once or twice. It stays with you.
  b[old] : Every day of my first year at work.
  : It stayed with me. I talk to every horse now, the way I wished somebody had talked to me then.

story the_burr_coat [topic=memories|festival|smalltalk]
  : I went to a wedding once in my best coat and came back with forty burrs in it. Forty!
  : I'd taken a short cut through a hedge. #ho#. Nobody looked at the bride; they all looked at me.
  ask : Have you ever been the talk of a wedding?
  b : Not for burrs. That's a story.
  b[friends] : I'd have counted them with you.
  : I picked them out at the feast, one by one, and told the table about each one. Forty stories.

story under_the_chapel [topic=weather|faith self.likes=thunder]
  : The best storm I ever heard, I was sitting in #chapel# with nobody else in it.
  : #thunder.capitalize# right over the roof, and the whole place hummed like a bell.
  ask : Do you know the feeling, when a building sings round you?
  b : I think I do. Once, in a barn.
  : That's the one. I sat there till it stopped and didn't say a word. Not one. Nobody believes me.

story the_kicker [topic=work|animals self.job=smith]
  : There was a carter's horse once that kicked every smith in the city. They brought it to me last.
  : I talked to it for an hour before I touched a foot. The weather, the price of oats, #birds#.
  ask : What do you think it did?
  b : Kicked you anyway? Or did it stand?
  : It stood! Bored stiff, I'd say. Never kicked again, not for me.

story father_forge [topic=memories|family self.away=yes self.from=larkfield self.age>=40]
  : My father kept a forge at #self.from_town#, by the sheep pens, and talked less than any wolf alive.
  : I swore I'd be different. #ho#. I've kept that promise every day since, loud.
  ask : Have you ever sworn to be nothing like your own folk?
  b : I did. I'm turning into them anyway.
  b[old] : Every pup does. Every old one finds out.
  : The quiet's come to me late. I sit in an empty chapel with it. I think that's his.

rule @shoe_cry
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=smith
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Shoes fitted, hoofs trimmed, nothing kicked! Bring #horse# in! | #ho#! Next horse, and mind its back end!

rule @nail_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=smith
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Eight of #nails#. Eight. Where's the eighth? | #oath#, there's a nail in my paw again.

rule @burr_bark
when concept=bark here.place=street|market|work
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another one. #burrs.capitalize#, always #burrs#. | Hold still. There. Got you, #ho#.

rule @thunder_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #ho#! Listen to that! Louder than me! | Go on, then. Shout. I'll shout back.

rule @rat_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats here.place=work|home
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Out of the oat bin! Out! | Rats again. Bold as you like.

rule @dawn_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Morning, birds! Morning, street! | #bellows.capitalize# up, kettle on. Here we go.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #ho#! Come in, come in. Shut the door, the rain gets in. #talk_open# | #greet#! What can a smith do for you?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#! #ho#! Come in. I've been saving things to tell you.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late, isn't it! Come in by #forge#. What's wanted?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. You've a look about you. Say what you came for, plainly.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=smith] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Horses, mostly: #nails#, shoes, trimming, and a lot of talking. | I shoe cart horses and talk to them while I do it. They don't seem to mind.
dlg @2 resident.job : A bit of everything, and loud with it. #job_busy# | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : #ho#! Couldn't be busier. I've horses tied up down the street.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=steady] : Steady! It keeps #forge# lit and my tea hot. That's all I ask.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : #bad.capitalize#, if I'm honest, and I am. The horses go elsewhere, or limp.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : #ho#, I heard this one at #forge#: from #world.news_from#, #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everybody at #gateroad# is on about #world.event_words#. I've talked of nothing else since breakfast.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'd tell you if I had any, believe me. | Nothing new, and I've asked every carter through #gateroad#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# For once in my life. | Not a thing! I'd have told you already, #ho#.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : #ho#, listen: they say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You didn't hear it from me. Everybody did.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#! Mind the step. | #farewell#! Come back and tell me how it went.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #ho#! Come in. Shoes, nails, a bit of ironwork. Look all you like, and talk while you do. | #greet#! Mind the hot end and have a look round.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#! Back again. #shop_offer#
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #shop_bare# I've shod every horse in the street and sold the rest. | Not much on the bench today. #ho#. Bring me iron and I'll buy it.
dlg @1 shop.prices : Iron's dear and coal's dearer. I don't set either. #shop_dear# | It's a fair sum for the work. I'll tell you exactly why, at length, if you ask.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#! | #shop_bye# And tell your friends.
graft resident.hub
choice You've a burr in your ruff. -> burr
node burr
say Have I? #ho#! There it is. I pick them out all day. Every hedge in Ridgemere has its eye on me. #saying#.
mood warm
free
choice Where do they all come from? -> burr_where
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node burr_where
say The bushes out past the east gate. I go for #berries# and come back with the hedge. Worth it, every time.
choice I'll leave you to them. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can you shoe a cart horse? [self.job=smith] -> shoe
node shoe
say Can I! Bring it round to the yard. Eight nails a shoe, and I'll talk to it the whole time so it doesn't fret.
mood keen
choice Why eight? -> shoe_eight
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
node shoe_eight
say Eight holds. Seven slips. Nine splits the hoof. Every smith knows it and I say it anyway. #saying#.
choice Thank you. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
